{
  "page": 18,
  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "Published in Transactions on Machine Learning Research (05/2025)",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        27.39893913269043,
        368.4171447753906,
        37.36153793334961
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For the state vector⃗s consisting of coordinates sk, the relation with the normalized state coordinate is then",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        83.85389709472656,
        540.120361328125,
        94.67189025878906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "given by ˆsk = 2 ˆFk(sk) −1. The states output from our dynamics model are unnormalized by the inverse",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        93.29090881347656,
        540.1589965820312,
        107.26657104492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "relation sk = ˆF −1",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        105.24592590332031,
        149.39810180664062,
        119.22152709960938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "k",
      "bbox": [
        137.81900024414062,
        113.9001693725586,
        142.05209350585938,
        120.09291076660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0000 1+ˆsk",
      "bbox": [
        149.8990020751953,
        102.86003112792969,
        173.2838134765625,
        113.64253997802734
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "2",
      "bbox": [
        162.7760009765625,
        114.36503601074219,
        166.7440948486328,
        120.52290344238281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\u0001",
      "bbox": [
        175.0590057373047,
        107.26647186279297,
        179.6218719482422,
        113.64253997802734
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".",
      "bbox": [
        179.625,
        108.82093811035156,
        182.3946075439453,
        117.66773223876953
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        135.94308471679688,
        79.67523956298828,
        146.55929565429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Model architectures and training details",
      "bbox": [
        92.82595825195312,
        135.94308471679688,
        311.2115783691406,
        146.55929565429688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E.1",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        161.6929473876953,
        86.9239730834961,
        170.53973388671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Diffusion models",
      "bbox": [
        97.8828353881836,
        161.6929473876953,
        173.66835021972656,
        170.53973388671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In this paper, we train 4 kinds of diffusion models: single-step diffusion action proposals, single-step diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        182.0019073486328,
        540.23095703125,
        191.96450805664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics models, multi-step diffusion action proposals, and multi-step diffusion dynamics models.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        193.95692443847656,
        500.8800048828125,
        203.91952514648438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We implement all 4 models as conditional diffusion models. For single-step diffusion action proposals, we use",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        211.88990783691406,
        540.2026977539062,
        221.85250854492188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "diffusion to model p(at|st); for single-step diffusion dynamics models, we use diffusion to model p(st +1|st, at);",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        223.8449249267578,
        541.38720703125,
        235.30252075195312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for multi-step diffusion action proposals, we use diffusion to model p(at:t+F −1|st); and for multi-step diffusion",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        235.79994201660156,
        540.0492553710938,
        246.61793518066406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics models we use diffusion to model p(st+1:t+F |st, at:t+F −1).",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        247.7559356689453,
        366.599609375,
        259.15277099609375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our diffusion implementation uses DDIM Song et al. (2020) with cosine schedule Nichol & Dhariwal (2021). We",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        265.68792724609375,
        540.1819458007812,
        275.6505432128906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "use transformers as our denoising network: for each conditional diffusion model, we embed the diffusion time",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        277.6429138183594,
        540.2177734375,
        287.60552978515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "using sinusoidal embeddings, project the time embeddings and each state and action (both for states/actions",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        289.5989074707031,
        540.2440795898438,
        299.5615234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "that are used as conditioning and for states/actions that are being modelled) to a shared token space with",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        301.55389404296875,
        540.219482421875,
        311.5165100097656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tokens of dimension 256, add Fourier positional embeddings with 16 Fourier bases to all tokens, and pass",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        313.5089111328125,
        540.2175903320312,
        323.4715270996094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "all the tokens through a number of transformer layers. We take the output tokens that correspond to the",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        325.4638977050781,
        540.2177124023438,
        335.426513671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "states/actions we are predicting, and project them back to the original state/action spaces.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        337.4189147949219,
        470.3145751953125,
        347.38153076171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For all our transformer layers, we use multi-headed attention with 8 heads, and 1024 total dimensions for",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        355.3518981933594,
        540.390380859375,
        365.31451416015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "query, key and value, and 2048 hidden dimensions for the MLP.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        367.3069152832031,
        350.42474365234375,
        377.26953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For all of our single-step diffusion action proposals, we use 5 diffusion timesteps and 2 transformer layers for",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        385.2398986816406,
        540.4208984375,
        395.2025146484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the denoiser.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        397.1949157714844,
        127.47175598144531,
        407.15753173828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For all of our single-step diffusion dynamics models, we use 3 diffusion timesteps and 2 transformer layers for",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        415.1278991699219,
        540.41650390625,
        425.09051513671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the denoiser.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        427.0829162597656,
        127.47175598144531,
        437.0455322265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For all of our multi-step diffusion action proposals, we use 32 diffusion timesteps and 5 transformer layers for",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        445.0158996582031,
        540.40673828125,
        454.978515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the denoiser.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        456.9709167480469,
        127.47175598144531,
        466.93353271484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "For all of our multi-step diffusion dynamics models, we use 10 diffusion timesteps and 5 transformer layers",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        474.9039001464844,
        540.1992797851562,
        484.86651611328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for the denoiser.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        486.8589172363281,
        142.72450256347656,
        496.821533203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "E.2",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        513.5699462890625,
        86.9239730834961,
        522.416748046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "One-step MLP dynamics models",
      "bbox": [
        97.8828353881836,
        513.5699462890625,
        246.0466766357422,
        522.416748046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We follow Argenson & Dulac-Arnold (2021) for the multi-layer perceptron (MLP) architecture of our one-step",
      "bbox": [
        71.49199676513672,
        533.8779296875,
        540.201171875,
        543.8405151367188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "dynamics model, and train it to approximate st+1 = f(st, at). We use only a single MLP. Hyperparameters",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        545.8328857421875,
        540.0945434570312,
        557.2904663085938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "for the model and training are summarized in Table 5.",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        557.7889404296875,
        309.97650146484375,
        567.7515258789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Hyperparameter",
      "bbox": [
        239.86199951171875,
        580.8250732421875,
        296.4962463378906,
        586.98291015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Value",
      "bbox": [
        338.6528625488281,
        580.8250732421875,
        358.053955078125,
        586.98291015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Number of FC layers",
      "bbox": [
        231.79400634765625,
        592.3800659179688,
        304.572509765625,
        598.5379028320312
      ],
      "direction": [
